# Pipeline output. The serving graph database is deliberately NOT in git: the
# nightly rebuild runs as a Fargate task and ships it to S3, and the conductor
# swaps it into the live path on the host (see infra/README.md). It was tracked
# via Git LFS until 2026-09; eleven committed rebuilds cost 9.9 GiB of LFS
# storage for a file nothing ever fetched.
data/*.db
data/*.bak-*
data/*.tmp.*.db-shm
data/*.tmp.*.db-wal

wiki/
slides

# Out-of-process rebuild: per-environment AWS IDs (see infra/build-job.conf.example)
infra/build-job.conf
